{"content":[{"c":["MACHBENAH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Evidently a place-name among the geographical names in the genealogy of Caleb and Judah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.49","r":"1Chr.2.49","rawR":"1Chr.2.49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.49","value":"1Chr.2.49"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:49"},"). It is followed by Gibea, which is probably the same town mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.57","r":"Josh.15.57","rawR":"Josh.15.57","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.57","value":"Josh.15.57"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 15:57"},"; thus, Machbenah was probably located in the eastern district of the hill country south of Hebron, an area where Calebites were to be expected."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Machbenah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.49","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.49","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.49"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 15:57","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.57","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.57","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.57"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"883bc4cc6b354fd00d7ce067756f4255d64dfc7c1e797a1870a0a94b8ddb352c","sourceItemName":"Machbenah","sourceItemOrder":26,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Machbenah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Machbenah*","title":"Machbenah*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}